## Why This Is Asked

This checks understanding of IND-CCA security and how to build practical, protocol-level defenses in modern cryptographic systems.

## Key Concepts

- IND-CCA and chosen-ciphertext resistance
- Encrypt-then-MAC vs MAC-then-Encrypt
- Nonce management, associated data, and MAC verification order
- Trade-offs: performance, ciphertext size, API surface

## Code Example

```javascript
function encrypt(plaintext, key) {
  const nonce = crypto.randomBytes(12);
  const cipher = crypto.createCipheriv('aes-128-gcm', key, nonce);
  const enc = Buffer.concat([cipher.update(plaintext, 'utf8'), cipher.final()]);
  const tag = cipher.getAuthTag();
  const payload = Buffer.concat([nonce, enc, tag]);
  const mac = crypto.createHmac('sha256', key).update(payload).digest();
  return { payload, mac };
}

function decrypt(payload, mac, key) {
  if (!verifyMac(mac, payload, key)) throw new Error('MAC fail');
  const nonce = payload.slice(0, 12);
  const enc = payload.slice(12, -16);
  const tag = payload.slice(-16);
  const decipher = crypto.createDecipheriv('aes-128-gcm', key, nonce);
  decipher.setAuthTag(tag);
  return Buffer.concat([decipher.update(enc), decipher.final()]);
}
```

## Follow-up Questions

- How would you audit for decryption oracle leakage?
- How would you enforce constant-time MAC checks and retry limits to prevent side channels?

## Why This Is Asked
Drift detection ensures model reliability and safe fallbacks in production scoring.

## Key Concepts
- Drift detection across model_version switches
- Telemetry fields: drift_flag, drift_reason, score_change_pct, last_model_version, last_score
- Fallback routing and drift alerts
- Observability and basic tests for drift, isolation, and rollback

## Code Example
```javascript
function checkDrift(currentScore, lastScore, lastModelVersion, currentModelVersion, threshold=0.15){
  const drift = Math.abs(currentScore - lastScore);
  const versionChanged = currentModelVersion !== lastModelVersion;
  const driftFlag = drift > threshold || versionChanged;
  const driftReason = versionChanged ? 'model_version_change' : (drift > threshold ? 'score_change' : 'none');
  const scoreChangePct = lastScore ? ((currentScore - lastScore) / Math.abs(lastScore)) * 100 : 0;
  return { driftFlag, driftReason, scoreChangePct };
}
```

## Follow-up Questions
- How would you store per-user drift telemetry at scale while preserving privacy?
- How would you tune the threshold and ensure safe fallbacks during rollout?

## Why This Is Asked
